*> PLB-C022 open-mode-mismatch: WRITE of a sequential file opened I-O,
*> which takes REWRITE only; an indexed file opened I-O takes WRITE.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. SEQIO.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT SEQ-FILE ASSIGN TO "seq.dat" ORGANIZATION LINE SEQUENTIAL
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
    SELECT IDX-FILE ASSIGN TO "idx.dat" ORGANIZATION INDEXED
        ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC RECORD KEY IS IDX-KEY
        FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  SEQ-FILE.
01  SEQ-REC             PIC X(10).
FD  IDX-FILE.
01  IDX-REC.
    05  IDX-KEY         PIC X(4).
    05  IDX-DATA        PIC X(6).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-FS               PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    OPEN I-O SEQ-FILE IDX-FILE
    READ SEQ-FILE
    REWRITE SEQ-REC
    WRITE SEQ-REC
    WRITE IDX-REC
    CLOSE SEQ-FILE IDX-FILE
    STOP RUN.
